  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mobilising Muslim Communities For Javan Rhino Conservation in Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Javan rhino (Rhinoceros sondaicus sondaicus) is critically endangered, with a single population of about 64 rhinos in Ujung Kulon National Park (UKNP), West Java, Indonesia. Threats to these rhinos include, poor local knowledge and awareness of UKNP, importance of conserving rhinos, and a negative attitude among local people towards UKNP. The project will empower religious and community leaders in 13 priority buffer zone villages to disseminate the teachings of a national Islamic edict (fatwa) calling on all Muslims to protect threatened species like the rhino. Project objectives and activities are: (1) Build capacity of 40 Muslim clerics to disseminate the fatwas teachings through mosques, prayer and community groups, and Islamic schools, reaching up to 9,000 people with rhino conservation messages; (2) Religious leaders help farmers and conservationists reach conservation commitments on land encroachment and buffalo grazing in UKNP; (3) Create fatwa teaching supplement and disseminate it to 10 Islamic schools near UKNP through capacity building for 20 teachers; and, (4) Create short awareness videos on the fatwa featuring Indonesias head cleric, for dissemination in mosques, community groups, schools and media.</narrative>
  </description>
